  {
    "id": "2843771496",
    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "Pokemon Mystery Dungeon - Treasure Town",
    "description": "TURN AUDIO RECORDING ON! It can cause an issue with the music player otherwise!\r\n\r\nPlease check out my second wallpaper!! https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3013457081\r\n\r\nBy using game assets from pokemon mystery dungeon: explorers of sky, I have made a wallpaper that feels alive and spans across two monitors!\r\n\r\nI merged a few different game scenes together to make them seemless and then created my own areas to fill in the blanks! Anyone that has played the game will know which areas are new and which are familiar.\r\n\r\nThere are numerous pokemon on screen, some stay, while some move around. There are even pokemon that enter the wallpaper and then leave again every 5 minutes.\r\n\r\nIncluded is a 77 song playlist composed by Anoyth (soundcloud: https://soundcloud.com/anoyth/sets/pmd2-orchestral-remaster?ref=clipboard&p=a&c=0)\r\n\r\nThe music player I use is by a steam user called Rhy.\r\n\r\nA big thank you to the devs of Sky Temple that made this possible as well as the artists that upload to the pmd sprite collab.\r\n\r\nAny and all feedback is welcome. This is my first wallpaper so I would like to keep updating it and even make more like this.\r\n\r\nNote: I'm not sure what wallpaper engine does when setting the default properties but having the alignment set to center should be the only change you might need to make. Feel free to change anything else, though how it looks will probably be strange as there are black bars around the edges and where the taskbar would be.\r\n\r\nNote2: The file size mostly comes from the songs that are included.\r\n\r\nFor the no music version go to: https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2843760391",
